WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.627
When a guided update reports insufficient space, start with

00:00:03.627 --> 00:00:04.941
the location that failed.

00:00:05.077 --> 00:00:08.619
In Appliance Operations, open Updates and review the storage

00:00:08.619 --> 00:00:09.293
allowance.

00:00:09.472 --> 00:00:13.227
In Ubuntu, use find mount to see which filesystem backs that

00:00:13.227 --> 00:00:13.788
path.

00:00:13.854 --> 00:00:17.608
If several paths share the root filesystem, growing root gives

00:00:17.608 --> 00:00:18.852
them all more room.

00:00:19.187 --> 00:00:22.294
First confirm a recoverable backup and an idle maintenance

00:00:22.302 --> 00:00:22.870
window.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.099
If the volume group already has enough free space, you can

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:27.655
skip the Prism resize.

00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:31.159
Otherwise, open the production virtual machine in Prism.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:34.381
Choose Update, then edit the existing disk.

00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:36.812
In Size, enter the new total.

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:40.874
To add forty gibibytes to an eighty gibibyte disk, enter one

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:41.811
hundred and twenty.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.875
Back in Ubuntu, check that the disk is larger.

00:00:44.947 --> 00:00:48.317
If it contains a partition, preview the change with grow part

00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:49.610
before applying it.

00:00:49.853 --> 00:00:54.333
For L V M, resize the physical volume, check free space, then

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:56.760
extend the logical volume and filesystem.

00:00:56.985 --> 00:01:00.227
For a standard partition, use the resize command that matches

00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:01.243
your filesystem.

00:01:01.465 --> 00:01:04.401
Check the mounted filesystem again and confirm that available

00:01:04.494 --> 00:01:05.538
space increased.

00:01:05.902 --> 00:01:09.358
Confirm the Orchestrator and PostgreSQL containers are healthy.

00:01:09.544 --> 00:01:13.803
In Updates, select the imported package and click Check Readiness.

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:17.045
Compare available space with the required allowance on every

00:01:17.053 --> 00:01:17.600
row.

00:01:17.736 --> 00:01:21.237
Proceed once all rows pass and overall readiness passes.

00:01:21.426 --> 00:01:25.181
If the resize causes a boot or filesystem problem, use the

00:01:25.181 --> 00:01:26.559
pre-change backup.

00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:29.646
Shrinking the expanded disk can truncate data.
